			},
			"date": "2023-12-19T17:53:17.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Regarding minimizing dependencies:</p><p>Once I started writing more and more Vanilla JS I feel like there's only a handful of cases I currently would reach out to a library:</p><p>- dates<br>- i18n<br>- parsing and generating files (CSV, XLS, PDF)<br>- Fetch (to a degree, because of boilerplate with Bearer tokens and abortion as well as isomorphic code)<br>- form and API validation (because I haven't figured out an elegant way here yet).</p><p>Other than that I think it's easier done without a framework.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
