		{
			"id": "111608709075250416",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@biilmann/111608708779213492",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matt Biilmann",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@biilmann",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/377/246/389/179/350/original/cc568205833e86e6.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-12-19T19:22:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The survey reflects of what our community responded.</p><p>Next is the largest framework in usage, clearly reflected in the survey.</p><p>But for the first time Next decreased in usage year over year (from 47% to 46%).</p><p>Astro jumped from 11% to 18% with 87% responding they want to use it more.</p><p>Eleventy dropped from 19% last year to 16% this year.</p><p>None of this is an attack on anyone, just data from our survey. </p><p>The rise of Astro is one of the most newsworthy bits of data that emerged.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
